  <section class="individual bg-darkblue pb-3 pt-5" id="step4">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="row">
        <div class="col-sm-12">
          <div class="title-container">
            <img src="https://individualogist.com/soul-flame-tarot/assets/img/title-bg-v2.png" alt="Snow" style="width:100%;">
            <h3 class="centered">As A <span class="archetype">Explorer</span>, These Are Your <span class="text-orange">Potential Career Paths</span></h3>
          </div>
          <p>Generally, the Explorer is a combination of introversion, intuitiveness, we-centeredness, and calmness. This makes up for strong career paths in relation to culinary, arts, and tourism. With their adventuristic nature, Explorers can blossom in these paths. And while these are suggestive of what you can pursue with your strengths, know that you should never limit yourself to them.</p>
          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/travel-blogger.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Travel Blogger</h5>
              <p>With their uniqueness, Explorers are best suited as travel bloggers. Because they have the natural knack to explore the world, they’ll find it natural to pursue a path that leads them to many places.</p>
              <p>As an Explorer, you are the epitome of a free spirit. You never allow something to limit you and your pursuits. Given such, having a boring 9-to-5 job is simply incomprehensible to you. While some Explorers tend to settle for such, truth be told, they are adventurers by heart.</p>
              <p>And for those who are truly living up to this, some Explorers will go full-time as travel bloggers. Experiencing the world while detailing its beauty and complexity, they will share photos and videos through social media. And as they relay their experiences to others, they can earn in the form of royalties or ad revenue.</p>
              <p>Even then, only quite a few are able to fully pursue this path. Should you choose to become a travel blogger, you can do so by aligning your job with it. For instance, choosing to become a flight attendant or an airplane pilot naturally enables you to travel the world for free.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Also, remember that other paths can lead to this. Doing business? Your leveraged income will allow you to become a travel blogger. Are you into sales? Salespeople usually hop from one city to another just to make that deal. As you live out your profession, you can align them with these different pursuits, which can unravel the world.</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/artist-outlaw.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Artist</h5>
              <p>Explorers are some of the best artists out there. With the limitlessness of their imagination, they are fit to create new forms of art. As a representation of their freedom and autonomy, their artworks become the very symbol of what they’re living for.</p>
              <p>As an Explorer, you can pursue this path. For instance, by becoming a traditional painter, you get to unravel the potentially boundless world of art. And as you dig deep into the various styles and niches, you can eventually create your own stroke.</p>
              <p>Furthermore, you can also explore the world of art in different ways. For example, doing architecture and interior design is a path that heavily involves a sense of art. Even when you don’t become a painter, exploring the world of design allows you to flap your wings and conceptualize an original blueprint. And as you do so, you leave your own mark, on top of being heftily paid by your clients.</p>
              <p>Lastly, art is also expressed through music. Just as how some people feel free, listening to music can ease one’s soul. How much more when you decide to create your own music?</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Yes, as an Explorer, you can choose to pursue the notes and make your own tune. Expressing your individuality as you do so, this path will unlock a different sense of freedom: one that is lived through the notes and tunes that you play.</p>

          <div class="row" style="margin-top: 3em;">
            <div class="col-sm-4 order-sm-2">
              <img src="../assets/images/chef.png" style="width: 100%;">
            </div>
            <div class="col-sm-8">
              <h5>Chef/Culinary Arts</h5>
              <p>The vast world of culinary and food art is known for its diversity and endlessness. With different cultures around the world, the number of dishes that it creates is almost endless to begin with. As such, this path of the palette is a good career for the Explorer.</p>
              <p>As a chef, you can explore the world through your tongue. By having a taste of the different flavors and the endless combinations that they create, you get to experience being in different places as you reminisce your travels. Just as how authentic restaurants replicate the experience of being in a particular city, this path will allow you to be free and autonomous.</p>
              <p>Add to that, culinary arts will also enable you to create your own dishes. As you travel the world, you will acquire knowledge about the traditions that each city has for their food. And as you bring that back home, you can begin adding your own twist to it.</p>

            </div>
          </div>
          <p>With this career path, you will find meaning and purpose. Heck, you can even become a cruise chef, allowing you to serve various kinds of dishes while exploring the world at the same time! Eventually, you can also cook for 5-star hotels or start your own restaurant chain, both of which will enable you financially.</p>
          <p>As long as you dedicate yourself to this craft, the possibilities are simply endless.</p>
          <p>But while your career prospects certainly glimmer with the hope of prosperity, there are uncomfortable truths about yourself that you will need to face. The first of which will be no more comforting, <span class="username"></span>, and it is this...</p>
